 a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot ID changed, and system, storage, mount, and data integrity recovered. The fixed after-executor boot identity independently matches the protocol's final identity.","limitations":["Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory LVM or mount state directly; those outcomes rely on detailed executor commands. The evidence is nevertheless coherent, includes the online transition, and is confirmed after restart."]}
